                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "TERRESTRIAL FATE: Based on a classification scheme(1), an estimated Koc value of 1.3X10+4(SRC), determined from a log Kow of 7.17(2) and a regression-derived equation(3), indicates that palmitic acid is expected to be immobile in soil(SRC). The estimated pKa of palmitic acid is 4.95(4), indicating that this compound will exist almost entirely in the anion form in the environment and anions generally do not adsorb more strongly to soils containing organic carbon and clay than their neutral counterparts(5). Volatilization of palmitic acid from moist soil surfaces is not expected to be an important fate process because anions do not volatilize. Palmitic acid is not expected to volatilize from dry soil surfaces(SRC) based upon a vapor pressure of 3.8X10-7 mm Hg at 25 °C(6). Palmitic acid reached 84% of its theoretical BOD in 28 days in a modified OECD screening test and accounting for poor water solubility(7), suggesting that biodegradation is expected to be an important environmental fate process in soil under certain environmental conditions(SRC).",
