                          "String": "AQUATIC FATE: Based on a classification scheme(1), an estimated Koc value of 1.3X10+4(SRC), determined from a log Kow of 7.17(2) and a regression-derived equation(3), indicates that palmitic acid is expected to adsorb to suspended solids and sediment(SRC). An estimated pKa of 4.95(4) indicates palmitic acid will exist almost entirely in the anion form at pH values of 5 to 9 and, therefore, volatilization from water surfaces is not expected to be an important fate process(SRC). According to a classification scheme(5), BCF of 60 in golden ide fish (Leuciscus idus melanotus) after 3 days exposure(6), suggests that bioconcentration in aquatic organisms is moderate(SRC). The concentration of palmitic acid decreased from 536 to 3.7 ug/L (half-life approximately 0.50 days) during a 29-day incubation period of freshwater(7), suggesting that biodegradation may be an important environmental fate process in water under certain conditions(SRC).",
