                    "Value": {
                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "URBAN/SUBURBAN: Sampling of particulate matter and gaseous pollutants was conducted for three weeks between October 7 and 29, 1976 in Belgium; palmitic acid was identified in the gas phase of urban air samples at an average concentration of 4.77 ug/1000 cu m and in particulate samples at an average concentration of 29.03 ug/1000 cu m(1). Palmitic acid was found at 88.4 ng/cu m in samples averaged from central Los Angeles, Azusa and Claremont, CA from samples taken Sept 1993(2). Palmitic acid had an average concentration of 72.6 ng/cu m from 4 urban sites from southern CA from samples taken Sept 8-9, 1993(3). In a study conducted from Sept 14-21, 1982 and Jan 25-31, 1983, air samples taken at three sites along the Niagra River were found to contain palmitic acid(4). Aerosol samples collected in the Tsukuba area northeast of Tokyo, Japan on April 28 and 29, 1985 contained palmitic acid in unknown concentrations(5). Aerosol samples were collected systematically throughout a complete annual cycle (1982) at four urban sites in southern California. Ambient annual concentrations of palmitic acid ranged from 118.3 to 140.5 ng/cu m(6). Palmitic acid was found in Vienna, Austria at 45 ng/cu m from samples taken June 1997(7). A southern CA atmospheric study gave concentrations of 47.4, 63.4, 33.1, 48.7 and 88.5 ng/cu m for Long Beach, Mira Loma, Riverside, San Dimas and Upland, respectively(8). Atmospheric samples taken Dec 26-28, 1995 and Jan 4-6, 1996 in Fresno, CA had palmitic acid in concentrations of 166 and 56.8 ng/cu m and samples taken in Bakersfield had 54.4 and 84.1 ng/cu m, respectively(9). Palmitic acid was found in atmospheric samples from North Birmingham, AL, Jefferson Street, GA, Gulfport, MS, Pensacola, FL and OLF#8, FL (a suburban site 20 km northwest of downtown Pensacola) at concentrations of 19.1, 11.4, 1.79, 8.82 and 1.55 ng/cu m, respectively(10). Palmitic acid was detected at a mean concentration of 310 ng/m cu, with range of 123-424 ng/m cu, in air samples collected between October and December of 2003 at seven locations in Hong Kong(11).",
