                        {
                          "String": "RURAL/REMOTE: Palmitic acid was found on aerosols obtained over the southern North Atlantic Ocean with a mean concentration of 6.7 ng/cu m and over Chacaltaya, Bolivia with a mean concentration of 3.6 ng/cu-m(1). Palmitic acid was measured in the aerosol form at 170.67, 51.47 and 35.57 ng/cu m at 6am - 12 pm, 12-6 pm and 6 pm-6 am, respectively, in samples taken July 27 to August 8, 1998 in the Pertouli area of the Agrafa Mountains, Greece(2) Analysis of the atmosphere in the Eggegebirge forest in North Rhine-Westflia, western Germany was found to contain palmitic acid, concentrations unknown(3). Palmitic acid was found at 7.8 ng/cu m from Sonnblick Observatory, Austria in samples taken May 1997(4). A southern CA atmospheric study gave palmitic acid concentrations of 8.6, 18.9, 33.1, 5.47, 20.6, 21.6 and 23.3 ng/cu m for Lompoc, Alpine, Atascadero, Lake Arrowhead, Lake Elsinore, Lancaster and Santa Maria, respectively(5). Atmospheric samples taken Dec 26-28, 1995 and Jan 4-6, 1996 in Kern Wildlife Refuge, CA had 9.58 and 10.4 ng/cu m of palmitic acid(6). Palmitic acid concentrations of 7.32, 1.94 and 2.08 ng/cu m were found in Centreville, AL, Yorkville, GA and Oak Grove, MS, respectively(7).",
