                        {
                          "String": "Palmitic acid was determined to be a volatile concentrate obtained from the Korean chamchwi plant (Aster scaber Thunb), concentration less than 0.02 % of total sample(1). Palmitic acid was identified as a volatile component of heated peanut oil(2). Palmitic acid has been identified in both roasted and boiled Chinese chestnuts (Castanea molissima)(3). The aroma concentrates of uncured beef were found to contain 0.32 mg/kg palmitic acid(4). The fine aerosol emission rate for palmitic acid from a frying hamburger (extra lean/regular), from a charbroiled hamburger (extra lean), and from a charbroiled hamburger (regular) was determined to be 14.2, 83.5, and 481.2 mg/kg, respectively(5). Palmitic acid has been identified in mutton and beef volatiles(6). Mature grains of 15 nonglutinous cultivars each of Indica, Sinica, Javanica, and Japonica brown rice collected in Japan and China in 1984 were determined to have an average of 19.56, 18.33, 15.20, and 16.79 % palmitic acid content, respectively(7). Palmitic acid has been identified as a volatile constituent of nectarine(8). Palmitic acid was found in paprika oleoresin at <0.1 mg/kg(9).",
